uld say that the uh this is  a weighted rate a weighted average of  these z-scores you could say that EPA OE  as uh you know trying to find a number  relative to expectation relative to a  League average that's the uh the most  leading driver of the model and  everything else it was a series of guest  and check to try to find out the weights  that best LED to high correlation high  high correlation to wins High stability  year to year and it had to pass the eye  test  it also had to to represent winning  football games so from the standpoint we  wanted by by grouping these scores into  five or five to ten range buckets we see  a very distinct pattern that the score  end of season had a very strong  relationship with how the team performed  on a win-loss basis  and then we wanted to measure the  validity of our of our metric compared  to the existing metrics out there so Pro  Football Focus which is another Advanced  football analytics service they have  their grades which are a little bit more  subjective you have human Charters  giving twos to negative twos on a per  play basis and they're doing a similar  aggregation and then ESPN's qbr now what  we tried to find is we optimize win  percentage optimize making playoffs  winning season and year-over-year  stability we don't want to necessarily  have too much year over year stability  in the sense of then we might have some  bias and that we only give Tom Brady the  same grade every week but the but the  idea is we we had a delicate balance and  a delicate business case where these are  all questions and all things that  Academia might not have to account for  but we do  and finally generate valid scores at any  sample size of past attempts so this is  the distribution of passing scores uh  both at the game and season level and  you can see that the normal distribution  uh the mean is right around our desired  mean and even if a game even if a  quarterback throws 14 passes he's still  within a range that we can understand  and digest at any sample of past  attempts  and again this is how the distribution  comes out  so to wrap it all up these are the top  10 quarterbacks from the Wild Card  Weekend these are not season ending  these are the Wild Card Weekend all five  quarterbacks that had the higher passing  score won the game  thank you so much  [Applause]
 

